From aeb6fb9b85bcb03841809baabe0fb90b6e88efb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:05:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add interactive Actions tab to the standalone GUI (gui/,
 version 2)

A fourth top-level tab discovers action servers, generates a goal editor
from the action's Goal definition, and sends, monitors and cancels goals.
All changes are under gui/.

- backend/ros_interfaces.py: resolve action types at run time, describe
  any message type as a schema, validate JSON values, build messages.
- backend/action_goals.py: the only module that acts on ROS. Goal records
  (UUID, state, feedback, result, timestamps) live in the gateway; action
  clients exist only while a goal is active; one-time request identifiers
  prevent duplicate goals; active goals are cancelled on normal shutdown
  unless --keep-goals-on-exit is given.
- backend/app.py: /api/v1/actions/* routes. The two POST routes need a
  loopback connection, local Host and Origin, a JSON body and the
  per-process session token; --read-only disables them. No publishing,
  service-call or parameter-write route exists. Contract version 1.1.
- frontend/tabs/actions/: server list, schema-driven form with JSON
  alternative, saved configurations (browser storage), confirmation
  dialog with a physical-action warning, monitor and history.
- tests: real fixture action servers (Fibonacci with feedback, cancel,
  reject, abort; LookupTransform with a nested goal); 25 HTTP tests and
  12 browser tests for actions. All version 1 tests still pass; the tab
  list test and the read-only-routes test were updated deliberately.

Verified in a cloud container with RoboStack Jazzy (90 tests passed);
not yet run on the target workstation. See gui/VERIFICATION.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TQArHBSyxZS2HP9MGqsusV
